<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ägeri</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ägerital</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ägeri is a valley in the Swiss canton of Zug around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-ageri">Lake Ägeri</a>, with the municipalities of Oberägeri and Unterägeri. It was one of the three rural communes, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menzingen">Menzingen</a> and Baar, that shared government of the old canton of Zug with the town. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-morgarten">Battle of Morgarten</a> in 1315 was fought near the southern end of its lake.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ageri.jpg" alt="Ägeri" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roland Zumbuehl · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oberaegeri-ZG.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
